--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Web portal npm packages
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The final clean installed-tree audit enumerated 267 entries: 266 third-party
packages and the private first-party root nereidsphere-portal@0.1.0. The root
is reported as UNLICENSED because package.json does not declare a license
field; it is not a third-party dependency and is governed by the repository
LICENSE.

The 266 installed third-party entries are grouped by their reported licenses:

    MIT (256)
        Direct runtime components include React, React DOM, Ant Design,
        @ant-design/icons, axios, i18next,
        i18next-browser-languagedetector, react-i18next, react-markdown,
        react-router-dom, remark-gfm, and Zustand. Vite and the MIT-licensed
        Babel, Rollup, unified/remark, Ant Design/rc-component, and other
        transitive packages used by the frontend build are also in this
        group.

    ISC (6)
        @ungap/structured-clone, electron-to-chromium, lru-cache, picocolors,
        semver, and yallist.

    Apache-2.0 (2)
        TypeScript and baseline-browser-mapping.

    BSD 3-Clause (1)
        source-map-js, Copyright (c) 2009-2011 Mozilla Foundation and
        contributors. All rights reserved.

    CC-BY-4.0 (1)
        caniuse-lite; see the attribution in section 1.

The complete lockfile contains 314 package entries including the first-party
root. Its metadata reports MIT (303), ISC (6), Apache-2.0 (2), BSD 3-Clause
(1), and CC-BY-4.0 (1); the root has no license field. The difference from
the installed-tree count is caused by platform-specific optional packages and
other lock entries not installed on the audit host.

License texts and package-specific copyright notices are available in the
corresponding package distributions and upstream repositories. The exact
versions are fixed by go.mod, go.sum, and web/package-lock.json.
